<title>NETHERLANDS: ING no comment on ScotAm bid report.</title>
<headline>ING no comment on ScotAm bid report.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch financial services group ING Groep NV (ING) said on Monday it had no comment on a report which named it as a bidder for life insurer Scottish Amicable.</p>
<p>&quot;As you know, we don't react to rumours,&quot; ING spokesman Ruud Polet told Reuters.</p>
<p>ING was one of a number of Continental European companies named by Britain's Sunday Times newspaper as possible bidders for Scottish Amicable, now facing a 1.4 billion stg bid from British retail banking group Abbey National.</p>
<p>Scottish Amicable plans to abandon its mutual status and seek a stock market listing.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
